  "cards": [
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "The push lane (new in v2)", "items": [
      "SNS keeps nothing, so an SQS subscription is what makes a past window re-readable at all",
      "The Receiver writes the batch to landing/ before deleting from the queue: a crash duplicates, never loses",
      "landing/ and bronze/ are prefixes in one bucket; the same Fetcher windows landing into bronze, so nothing downstream changes"] },
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Stateless compute on EKS", "items": [
      "Everything in ap-southeast-2: Go workers, the Receiver, dbt workers, PgBouncer and BI are Deployments",
      "Temporal drives both lanes — MaterialiseWindow on the Go workers, BuildMarts on the dbt workers",
      "Go binaries stay CGO-free: they write Parquet and read marts over Postgres wire"] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Two Postgres roles", "items": [
      "RDS Postgres holds the DuckLake catalog and Temporal persistence: plain tables, managed, Multi-AZ",
      "The serving Postgres runs pg_duckdb, which RDS does not offer, so it is a pod; it holds no durable state",
      "Redshift Spectrum can still read the same bronze bucket if the named triggers are hit"] }
